.TH OPENEIGRPD 8 "November 2026" "OpenEIGRP" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
openeigrpd \- native Linux EIGRP daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B openeigrpd
.RI [ -f " path" ]
.RI [ -s " socket" ]
.RI [ -t ]
.RI [ -V ]
.RI [ -h ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The native OpenEIGRP daemon is packaged together with
.BR oectl (8)
and the configuration validator
.BR openeigrpd-config (8).
The systemd unit is installed disabled and is never started by a fresh
package installation. An administrator must configure routing and explicitly
run
.B systemctl enable --now openeigrpd
before it can exchange EIGRP packets or modify kernel routes.
.PP
The service passes a per-service protected copy of
.B /etc/openeigrpd.conf
using the
.B -f
option. The daemon runs in the foreground and processes Linux Netlink,
raw protocol-88 packet events and management IPC while the portable core
owns RTP, timers and DUAL. It needs CAP_NET_RAW and CAP_NET_ADMIN for
routing. SIGTERM and SIGINT trigger orderly shutdown.
SIGHUP is rejected without applying a partial live configuration.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI -f " path"
Read the named-mode configuration file (default /etc/openeigrpd.conf).
.TP
.BI -s " socket"
Override the Unix management socket (default /run/openeigrpd/control.sock).
The parent directory must exist, be owned by root or the daemon user,
and not be writable by group or other users.
.TP
.B -t
Validate configuration syntax without opening raw sockets or changing routes.
.TP
.B -V
Print the portable OpenEIGRP release identifier and exit.
.TP
.B -h
Print command help and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/openeigrpd.conf
Root-owned, mode 0600 dpkg conffile.
.TP
.B /run/openeigrpd/control.sock
Read-only management control socket. Grant membership in the
.B openeigrpctl
group to authorized observers; the daemon creates the socket
with group access (0660).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR oectl (8),
.BR openeigrpd.conf (5),
.BR systemctl (1)
